## Every execve a person started, tagged so that vigil reads its own records.
##
##   auid!=unset              only what a login session is behind. `auid` is the loginuid: the
##                            account that logged in, kept across su and sudo. A process that
##                            no session started — a systemd service, a cron job, a container,
##                            anything auditd itself spawns — has no loginuid at all, which the
##                            kernel writes as 4294967295 and this filter as `unset`.
##
##   arch=b64 and arch=b32    both: a 32-bit process walks past a b64-only rule. b32 is second
##                            because a kernel without 32-bit support refuses it and augenrules
##                            reports the refusal. Keep the order.
##   -k vigil_exec            the tag vigil selects its own records by. Your rules are untouched.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S execve -F auid!=unset -k vigil_exec
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S execve -F auid!=unset -k vigil_exec
